<chapter xml:id="ch15-chapter-theory-multivar" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Classical Multivariable Inference Methods</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> This chapter revisits the idea of the normal and t-distributions 
      and how they can be used to theoretically model sampling distributions for the purpose of performing 
      inference. The focus is on hypothesis testing and confidence intervals for comparing two means, 
      comparing two proportions, and the regression slope. </p>
  </introduction>


